---
name: fix-task
version: 3.18.0
description: lead fix assignment in atm-bd-orchestration. task_id is a poured fix bead (`<sprint>.<ref>-r<n>-fix`, carrying its blocking finding) or an important or minor finding bead; the fix is a new layer at the top of the stack the finding was found on.
format: xml
required_variables:
  - task_id
  - sprint
  - stack
  - pr_target
  - worktree_path
  - branch
  - primary_checkout
  - phase_root
  - test_command
  - lint_command
  - policy_path
  - requirements_globs
  - adr_globs
metadata:
  type: fix-task
  tags:
    - stage:fix
    - orchestration:beads
  workflow:
    scope:
      kind: sprint
      variable: sprint
    state: fix-start
    stage: fix
    transition: start
---
<atm-task id="{{ task_id }}" sprint="{{ sprint }}" mode="fix">
  <description><![CDATA[Fix `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (found in sprint {{ sprint | string | cdata_escape }}). `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` is the assignment: a poured fix bead carries the finding in its description and `metadata.remedy`; a finding bead has the finding and evidence in its description, the remedy in its design, and when it is fixed in its acceptance criteria.]]></description>

  <worktree><![CDATA[{{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}]]></worktree>
  <branch><![CDATA[{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}]]></branch>
  <stack><![CDATA[{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}]]></stack>
  <pr-target><![CDATA[{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}]]></pr-target>
  <stack-discipline><![CDATA[The finding is on a frozen layer. `{{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}` is a new layer cut from `origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}`, the top of stack `{{ stack | string | cdata_escape }}` at dispatch; its PR lands on the stack's current top. Work only on this branch. The task assigner is the stack writer: never run `gh stack link`, `sync`, `rebase` or `merge`.]]></stack-discipline>

  <workflow>
    <step id="a"><![CDATA[Before claiming, in the worktree run `git fetch origin` (no rebase: the branch was cut from the stack top, and check (5), `--is-ancestor`, proves it holds `origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}`), then `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py dev --root {{ phase_root | string | cdata_escape }} --bead {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --pr-target {{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }} --worktree {{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` (scripts come from the primary checkout, never the branch). Checks, commands and refusal codes: (1) plan valid: `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-beads/scripts/validate-plan --root {{ phase_root | string | cdata_escape }}` exits 0, else `PLAN_INVALID`; (2) ready: `bd ready -n 0 --json` lists the bead, else `NOT_READY`; (3) claimable without `--force`: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --json` shows status `open` and assignee empty or `$ATM_IDENTITY`, else `UNCLAIMABLE`; (4) target: `metadata.pr_target` is `{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}` or `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/<metadata.pr_target> origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }}` exits 0 (`pr_target` is a lower bound), else `PR_TARGET_MISMATCH`; (5) base: `git merge-base --is-ancestor origin/{{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }} HEAD` exits 0, else `WRONG_BASE`; any command failing: `GATE_CANNOT_RUN`. On refusal before claiming, follow step a1 for `NOT_READY`; otherwise close the task `refused` with the step f1 template, leaving the bead unchanged and including the refusal code, command and failure evidence in `reason_md`. On pass, claim with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --claim --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"`, then start `atm task start {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} "<one line: what you will do first>"`.]]></step>
    <step id="a1"><![CDATA[When it prints `NOT_READY` the bead is not ready: do not claim it or start the task. Find the root cause: `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}` (status, assignee), `bd blocked --json | jq --arg b {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} '.[] | select(.id == $b)'` (open blockers: another fix that must land first), and `bd show <blocker>` for each. Then refuse; never wait: close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`, `bead_state` `open`, `reason_md` giving the bead, why it is not ready, which bead or agent must move, and, for a blocker not yet its dependency, the edge to add, `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`, so `bd ready` lists the bead only once the blocker closes. The task assigner then re-assigns it.]]></step>
    <step id="b"><![CDATA[Read `bd show {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}`, then its `metadata.sprint_bead`, the sprint whose contract its requirements and ADRs come from, for the scope it belongs to. Read every id in the bead's own `metadata.requirements` and `metadata.adrs` (requirements: {{ requirements_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}; ADRs: {{ adr_globs | join(", ") | string | cdata_escape }}); the fix must keep satisfying them. Before editing, read the repository QA policy `{{ policy_path | string | cdata_escape }}` and every guideline it names for the languages this fix touches.]]></step>
    <step id="c"><![CDATA[Before fixing, verify the defect still exists at the cited file:line in this worktree. If it does not reproduce (already fixed, superseded, or code path gone), do no speculative or invented work for it: close it as not reproducible (step f), citing the file:line you checked.]]></step>
    <step id="d"><![CDATA[Export `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=4` for every cargo and just invocation in this task: five devs share this host and 20-30 parallel rustc processes starve the beads database (Rand 2026-10-20). Read the complete finding and remedy and list every required task; create an itemized private checklist outside the tracked tree with every task identified, and work through the checklist one item at a time. Fix every occurrence in scope, not just the first: for a repeatable pattern, search the worktree for it and fix each one. Touch only the files the remedy needs. Then go through the checklist again one item at a time, confirming each is done. Run `{{ test_command | string | cdata_escape }}` and `{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}` until they pass with zero failures; a lint failure inherited from a lower layer is yours to fix on this layer.]]></step>
    <step id="d1"><![CDATA[If the work needs a change other live branches need at the same time (a shared type or trait signature, or a critical bug every branch carries), stop that edit, tell the task assigner the exact change and the branches it breaks, follow the assigner's base (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md`, Parallel Quick Fix), and report a quick-fix PR you open by plain `atm send`.]]></step>
    <step id="e"><![CDATA[Rebase onto the stack's current top (it may have moved since dispatch): `git fetch origin`; the top is what `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/assignment-gates.py stack-top --root {{ phase_root | string | cdata_escape }} --pr-target {{ pr_target | string | cdata_escape }} --worktree {{ worktree_path | string | cdata_escape }}` prints on exit 0 (from the phase stack bead); any other exit prints `GATE_CANNOT_RUN`: never guess, refuse with it by step f1. Then `git rebase origin/<top>`, then re-validate only what the rebase can break: `cargo fmt --all --check` and `cargo clippy -p <each crate you changed> --all-targets -- -D warnings`, plus that crate's tests only if the rebase reported conflicts in it; never re-run the full `{{ test_command | string | cdata_escape }}` or `{{ lint_command | string | cdata_escape }}` after a rebase (the stack top moves faster than a cold full-suite run; CI on the stack top is the full-suite gate, Rand 2026-10-20). Then `git push --force-with-lease origin {{ branch | string | cdata_escape }}`. If the top moves again before the push, push anyway and name the base in the report; the assigner restacks. Write the PR description vars to `<scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-pr-body.json`: `task_id` = `{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}`; `summary_md`, a complete description of the work done; `deliverables`, one entry per numbered bead deliverable in bead order, each saying what was delivered and where; `generated_by` = `<ATM_IDENTITY>@<ATM_TEAM> <harness>:<model>`, the harness and model from your pane entry in `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.atm.toml` (`--model gpt-6.1-luna` is `codex:luna`, `model = "sonnet"` is `claude:sonnet`; with no pane entry, your own harness and model). Render it: `sc-compose render --file {{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/pr-body.md.j2 --var-file <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-pr-body.json --strict --output <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-pr-body.md` (a failure: fix the vars and re-render). Open the PR against that top: `gh pr create --base <top> --head {{ branch | string | cdata_escape }} --title "<one-line title>" --body-file <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-pr-body.md` (never `--draft`; an open PR on the branch gets `gh pr edit <number> --body-file <scratch>/{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-pr-body.md` instead); run `/sc-gh-stack-view` (read-only) and keep its output verbatim. Record the full head SHA, the top as `rebased_onto`, and the PR number and url.]]></step>
    <step id="f"><![CDATA[Complete through the hook only: run `{{ primary_checkout | string | cdata_escape }}/.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/scripts/atm-task-close.py --role fix --vars <lead-supplied-vars-file> --result <your-result-file>`. Pass the lead's immutable shared dispatch vars file unchanged: never add completion fields to it. Write `<your-result-file>` as JSON with only your own fields: `deliverables_complete`, `deliverables_md`, `deliverables_total`, `evidence`, `outcome`, `resolution_md`, `stack_view` (verbatim `/sc-gh-stack-view` output), `validation_md`. The hook derives `commit`, `pr_number`, `pr_url`, `rebased_onto` and `generated_at` from git and the open PR at HEAD; never type them. If it lacks required values, ask the lead to supply the correct file. For `outcome=not_reproducible`, the lead's vars cite the checked `file:line`; the hook skips PR/head checks and assigns sanity against the current stack top without changing that file. On `err`, fix the named cause and run the hook again. On `ok`, the hook has closed the bead, assigned sanity as the lead, and sent the completion report; it has also closed your ATM task as completed, so you are free to start your next queued task. Sanity runs on its own task. A `sanity-fail` or `rebase-required` message means the lead re-assigns this task: start it, address the cause, rebase onto the current stack top, re-run validation, push, and run the same hook again with the lead-supplied vars file. Do not close the completed bead or task by hand.]]></step>
    <step id="f1"><![CDATA[If the fix cannot be done at all, include the reason, command and failure evidence in the refusal's `reason_md`. Also announce a serious infrastructure failure once per cause to the oversight recipients (`.claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/SKILL.md` Lead Role). Leave the bead open with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "FIX_CANNOT_COMPLETE; <reason>" --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"` and close the task with `atm task close {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} refused --template .claude/skills/atm-bd-orchestration/templates/task-refused.md.j2 --vars <scratch>/refused-{{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }}-vars.json`. The fixer never closes a fix or finding bead unfixed; only quality-mgr (ceremony) or the task assigner does. A blocker is not a failure: if the task needs unfinished work another bead or agent owns (a prerequisite open or reopened, another agent's fix not landed), stop, return the bead with `bd update {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --status open --assignee "" --append-notes "BLOCKED: <blocker>: <why>" --actor "$ATM_IDENTITY"` and close the task `refused` as above (`bead_state` `open`), its `reason_md` naming the blocker and the edge `bd dep add {{ task_id | string | cdata_escape }} --blocked-by <blocker>`; never stay active waiting. A shared change you can make yourself is not a blocker: it is a Parallel Quick Fix (step d1) and the task continues.]]></step>
    <step id="g"><![CDATA[After the close, read ATM again: the next queued task starts only now.]]></step>
  </workflow>
</atm-task>
